(function(E){ const x = E["exam-06"] = E["exam-06"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x06-r1"] = {"id":"x06-r1","patterns":["RA-nature","GT1-ads","PARA-cause"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes on a description with one word or a number from the passage, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN about what has been done to protect the animal.","tr":"Bu derste bir betimleme üzerine notları metinden bir kelime ya da bir sayıyla tamamlamayı ve hayvanı korumak için yapılanlar hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌های یک توصیف را با یک کلمه یا یک عدد از متن کامل کنی و درباره‌ی کارهایی که برای حفاظت از جانور شده بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match statements to five short listings, using some letters more than once, and to complete a flow-chart with one word from a step-by-step guide.","tr":"Bu derste bazı harfleri birden fazla kullanarak ifadeleri beş kısa ilanla eşleştirmeyi ve adım adım bir rehberden tek kelimeyle bir akış şemasını tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را با پنج آگهیِ کوتاه جور کنی، طوری که بعضی حرف‌ها بیش از یک بار بیایند، و یک نمودار مراحل را با یک کلمه از یک راهنمای قدم‌به‌قدم کامل کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: an animal and its protection","tr":"Reading Passage 1: bir hayvan ve korunması","fa":"Reading Passage 1: یک جانور و حفاظت از آن"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete notes on a description with one word or a number from the passage, and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN about what has been done to protect the animal.","tr":"Bu derste bir betimleme üzerine notları metinden bir kelime ya da bir sayıyla tamamlamayı ve hayvanı korumak için yapılanlar hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یادداشت‌های یک توصیف را با یک کلمه یا یک عدد از متن کامل کنی و درباره‌ی کارهایی که برای حفاظت از جانور شده بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~760"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a giant river fish","tr":"Bu sınav: dev bir nehir balığı","fa":"این آزمون: یک ماهی غول‌پیکر رودخانه‌ای"},"intro":{"en":"Animals and their protection are the most common Passage 1 subject. The first half usually describes the animal; the second explains the threat and the response. Cause-and-change words carry most of the statements.","tr":"Hayvanlar ve korunmaları en sık çıkan Passage 1 konusudur. İlk yarı genelde hayvanı anlatır; ikinci yarı tehdidi ve buna verilen karşılığı açıklar. İfadelerin çoğunu neden ve değişim kelimeleri taşır.","fa":"جانوران و حفاظت از آن‌ها رایج‌ترین موضوع Passage 1 هستند. نیمه‌ی اول معمولاً جانور را توصیف می‌کند و نیمه‌ی دوم خطر و واکنش به آن را. بیشتر جمله‌ها را کلمه‌های علت و تغییر می‌سازند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-nature","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A large animal under threat","tr":"Tehdit altındaki büyük bir hayvan","fa":"جانوری بزرگ در خطر"},"asks":{"en":"A natural history in two halves: first the animal itself (its body, food and breeding), then why it declined and what is being done to protect it. The notes test the first half, the statements the second.","tr":"İki yarıdan oluşan bir doğa tarihi: önce hayvanın kendisi (bedeni, beslenmesi ve üremesi), sonra neden azaldığı ve onu korumak için ne yapıldığı. Notlar ilk yarıyı, ifadeler ikinci yarıyı ölçer.","fa":"روایتی از طبیعت در دو نیمه: اول خودِ جانور (بدن، غذا و تولیدمثل) و بعد اینکه چرا کم شد و برای حفاظتش چه می‌کنند. یادداشت‌ها نیمه‌ی اول را می‌سنجند و جمله‌ها نیمه‌ی دوم را."},"fields":["Body","Feeding","Breeding","Why it declined","Protection","The future"],"words":[{"a":"instead of scales","b":"its body is protected by plates","tr":"pullar yerine","fa":"به جای فلس"},{"a":"feeds on","b":"eats / its diet consists of","tr":"... ile beslenir","fa":"تغذیه می‌کند از"},{"a":"the bottom of the river","b":"the river bed","tr":"nehir tabanı","fa":"کف رودخانه"},{"a":"matures slowly","b":"breeds for the first time late in life","tr":"geç olgunlaşır","fa":"دیر بالغ می‌شود"},{"a":"upstream","b":"towards the source of the river","tr":"akıntıya karşı, yukarı","fa":"خلاف جریان، بالادست"},{"a":"valued","b":"what they wanted most / prized","tr":"değer verilen","fa":"باارزش"},{"a":"cut off from","b":"could no longer reach","tr":"... ile bağlantısı kesildi","fa":"دسترسی‌اش قطع شد"},{"a":"banned","b":"made illegal / no longer allowed","tr":"yasaklandı","fa":"ممنوع شد"},{"a":"continues","b":"still happens / has not ended","tr":"devam ediyor","fa":"ادامه دارد"},{"a":"survival rate","b":"how many stay alive","tr":"hayatta kalma oranı","fa":"نرخ زنده ماندن"},{"a":"released","b":"put into the river / set free","tr":"serbest bırakıldı","fa":"رها شد"},{"a":"fell by nine-tenths","b":"dropped by 90 per cent","tr":"onda dokuz azaldı","fa":"نُه‌دهم کم شد"}],"traps":[{"en":"A partial success: \"The new law has helped, but hunting still goes on in remote areas.\" A statement saying the problem has ended is FALSE.","tr":"Kısmi bir başarı: \"Yeni yasa işe yaradı ama uzak bölgelerde avlanma hâlâ sürüyor.\" Sorunun bittiğini söyleyen bir ifade FALSE olur.","fa":"موفقیتی ناقص: «قانون تازه کمک کرد، اما در مناطق دورافتاده شکار هنوز ادامه دارد». جمله‌ای که بگوید مشکل تمام شده FALSE است."},{"en":"A detail that is not there: the text describes a new structure but not who paid for it. A statement about the money is NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Orada olmayan bir ayrıntı: metin yeni bir yapıyı anlatıyor ama parasını kimin ödediğini söylemiyor. Parayla ilgili bir ifade NOT GIVEN olur.","fa":"جزئیاتی که نیامده: متن یک سازه‌ی تازه را توصیف می‌کند، اما نمی‌گوید پولش را چه کسی داد. جمله‌ای درباره‌ی پول NOT GIVEN است."},{"en":"Notes with numbers: copy the figure exactly, with no units if the unit is printed.","tr":"Sayılı notlar: rakamı aynen kopyala; birim yazılıysa birimi ekleme.","fa":"یادداشت‌های عددی: عدد را دقیقاً کپی کن و اگر واحد چاپ شده، واحد را ننویس."}],"example":{"text":"\"For generations the bird was hunted, but never mainly for food. It was its long tail feathers that people wanted, for hats.\"","item":"Statement: The bird was hunted mainly for its meat.","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Never mainly for food... its long tail feathers\" contradicts the statement.","tr":"\"Hiçbir zaman esas olarak yiyecek için değil... uzun kuyruk tüyleri\" ifadeyle çelişiyor.","fa":"«هیچ‌وقت عمدتاً برای غذا نبود... پرهای بلند دُمش» با جمله تناقض دارد."}}},{"id":"RA-nature-p1","ctx":["RA-nature"],"title":{"en":"Natural history accounts","tr":"Doğa tarihi anlatıları","fa":"روایت‌های تاریخ طبیعی"},"asks":{"en":"A factual account of an animal, a plant or a natural place: how it lives, how it was discovered, why it declined and how it is protected. Statements test single facts; the notes follow the order of the text.","tr":"Bir hayvan, bitki ya da doğal bir yer hakkında bilgilendirici bir metin: nasıl yaşadığı, nasıl keşfedildiği, neden azaldığı ve nasıl korunduğu. İfadeler tek tek bilgileri sınar; notlar metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"متنی اطلاعاتی درباره‌ی یک حیوان، یک گیاه یا یک مکان طبیعی: چطور زندگی می‌کند، چطور کشف شد، چرا کم شد و چطور از آن حفاظت می‌شود. جمله‌ها اطلاعات جزئی را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The species was first described in the 1800s.","Its numbers have fallen since the 1950s.","It is found only on one island.","Farmers consider it a pest.","Notes: Diet · Habitat · Threats · Protection"],"words":[{"a":"declined","b":"fell in number / became scarcer","tr":"azaldı","fa":"کم شد"},{"a":"disappeared","b":"became extinct / died out","tr":"yok oldu","fa":"از بین رفت"},{"a":"only","b":"exclusively / nowhere else","tr":"yalnızca","fa":"فقط"},{"a":"first","b":"the earliest / originally","tr":"ilk","fa":"اولین"},{"a":"increased","b":"rose / grew / expanded","tr":"arttı","fa":"افزایش یافت"},{"a":"protect","b":"conserve / save from","tr":"korumak","fa":"حفاظت کردن"},{"a":"harmful","b":"damaging / a threat to","tr":"zararlı","fa":"مضر"},{"a":"common","b":"widespread / found in many places","tr":"yaygın","fa":"رایج"},{"a":"scientists","b":"researchers / biologists","tr":"bilim insanları","fa":"دانشمندان"},{"a":"uncertain","b":"it remains unclear / not yet known","tr":"belirsiz","fa":"نامعلوم"},{"a":"caused by","b":"the result of / due to","tr":"... yüzünden","fa":"ناشی از"},{"a":"brought in","b":"introduced by humans","tr":"dışarıdan getirilmiş","fa":"وارد شده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Hedging: \"may\", \"some researchers believe\". A statement that turns this into a fact is usually FALSE or NOT GIVEN; compare carefully.","tr":"Temkinli dil: \"may\", \"bazı araştırmacılara göre\". Bunu kesin bilgiye çeviren bir ifade genelde FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olur; dikkatle karşılaştır.","fa":"زبان محتاطانه: «may»، «بعضی پژوهشگرها معتقدند». جمله‌ای که این را به واقعیت قطعی تبدیل کند معمولاً FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است؛ دقیق مقایسه کن."},{"en":"\"Only\", \"always\", \"never\" in a statement: one exception in the text makes it FALSE.","tr":"İfadede \"only\", \"always\", \"never\": metindeki tek bir istisna onu FALSE yapar.","fa":"«only»، «always»، «never» در جمله: یک استثنا در متن آن را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"Notes: two numbers or dates sit close together. The heading decides which one you need.","tr":"Notlar: iki sayı ya da tarih yan yanadır. Hangisinin gerektiğine başlık karar verir.","fa":"یادداشت‌ها: دو عدد یا تاریخ نزدیک هم‌اند. عنوان تعیین می‌کند کدام را لازم داری."}],"example":{"text":"The hazel dormouse was once found in woods across most of England. Its range has shrunk by about half since 1900, mainly because the hedges that linked woodlands were removed. Most surviving populations are now in the south.","item":"Statement: The dormouse has always lived only in the south of England.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Once found in woods across most of England\" contradicts \"always... only in the south\".","tr":"\"Bir zamanlar İngiltere’nin çoğunda\" bulunması, \"her zaman... yalnızca güneyde\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«زمانی در جنگل‌های بیشتر انگلستان بود» با «همیشه... فقط در جنوب» در تضاد است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Notes first, then seven statements","tr":"Önce notlar, sonra yedi ifade","fa":"اول یادداشت، بعد هفت جمله"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-6: notes on the animal, with ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage. Questions 7-13: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on the rest of the passage. Both sets follow the order of the text. Spend about 20 minutes.","tr":"Soru 1-6: hayvan hakkında, metinden ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER ile notlar. Soru 7-13: metnin geri kalanı üzerine TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. İki grup da metnin sırasını izler. Yaklaşık 20 dakika ayır.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۶: یادداشت درباره‌ی جانور، با ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER از متن. سؤال‌های ۷ تا ۱۳: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی بقیه‌ی متن. هر دو گروه ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند. حدود ۲۰ دقیقه وقت بگذار."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Read the note headings (body, food, breeding) and find those paragraphs.","tr":"Not başlıklarını (beden, beslenme, üreme) oku ve o paragrafları bul.","fa":"عنوان یادداشت‌ها (بدن، غذا، تولیدمثل) را بخوان و آن پاراگراف‌ها را پیدا کن."},{"en":"For each gap, find a paraphrase of the words around it and copy one word or one figure.","tr":"Her boşluk için etrafındaki kelimelerin başka sözcüklerle söylenişini bul ve bir kelime ya da bir rakam kopyala.","fa":"برای هر جای خالی، بیانِ دیگرِ کلمه‌های اطرافش را پیدا کن و یک کلمه یا یک عدد کپی کن."},{"en":"For each statement, find its one sentence and check the details: dates, completely, all, still.","tr":"Her ifade için tek cümlesini bul ve ayrıntıları kontrol et: tarihler, completely, all, still.","fa":"برای هر جمله، همان یک جمله‌ی متن را پیدا کن و جزئیات را چک کن: تاریخ‌ها، completely، all، still."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One note, step by step","tr":"Bir not, adım adım","fa":"یک یادداشت، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the notes. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer.","text":"\"The young turtles stay in the nest for about 60 days before they dig their way out at night.\"","item":"Note: Young stay in the nest for about ___ days","answer":"60","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: the sentence about the young and the nest.","tr":"Yeri bul: yavrular ve yuvayla ilgili cümle.","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: جمله‌ای درباره‌ی بچه‌ها و لانه."},{"en":"\"about\" and \"days\" are printed in the note, so only the number is missing.","tr":"Notta \"about\" ve \"days\" yazılı, yani yalnızca sayı eksik.","fa":"«about» و «days» در یادداشت چاپ شده‌اند، پس فقط عدد جا افتاده."},{"en":"Write 60 as figures. \"about 60 days\" would repeat printed words.","tr":"60’ı rakamla yaz. \"about 60 days\" yazılı kelimeleri tekrarlar.","fa":"۶۰ را با رقم بنویس. «about 60 days» کلمه‌های چاپ‌شده را تکرار می‌کند."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"A bridge for the animals was built in 2018.\" Statement: \"The bridge was paid for by the government.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The year is given, but nothing is said about who paid.","tr":"Yıl veriliyor ama kimin ödediği hakkında bir şey söylenmiyor.","fa":"سال آمده، اما درباره‌ی اینکه چه کسی پول داد چیزی گفته نشده."}},"remember":{"en":"Copy one word or figure exactly for notes; for statements, check every detail against one sentence.","tr":"Notlar için bir kelimeyi ya da rakamı aynen kopyala; ifadelerde her ayrıntıyı tek bir cümleyle karşılaştır.","fa":"برای یادداشت یک کلمه یا عدد را دقیقاً کپی کن؛ برای جمله‌ها همه‌ی جزئیات را با یک جمله مقایسه کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"The giant of the Karva","tr":"Karva’nın devi","fa":"غول رود کاروا"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-nature"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"The giant of the Karva\n\nFor most of its length, the Karva is a slow, brown river that winds across a wide plain before emptying into an inland sea. Few of the people who cross its bridges each day know that it is home to one of the largest freshwater fish in the world. The Karva sturgeon can grow to four metres in length and live for more than eighty years. It has existed in something like its present form for millions of years, long before the river took its current course, which is why biologists sometimes call it a living fossil.\n\nAt first sight the sturgeon looks more like a reptile than a fish. Instead of scales, its body is protected by five rows of hard, bony plates known as scutes, which run from head to tail. It has no teeth. Instead, it feeds by swimming slowly along the river bed and sucking up whatever it finds there, using four sensitive whiskers beneath its mouth to detect food in the mud. Its diet consists mainly of insect larvae, worms and shellfish, although large adults will also take small fish. A fully grown sturgeon has very few natural enemies.\n\nLike salmon, the sturgeon spends most of its life in one place and travels to another to breed. Adults feed in the shallow waters of the inland sea, but they return to the river to lay their eggs. The species is slow to mature: females usually breed for the first time when they are about 20 years old, and even then only every three or four years. When the time comes, they swim up to 900 kilometres upstream to reach the fast-flowing stretches near the mountains, where they lay their eggs on beds of pebbles. The current keeps the eggs supplied with oxygen until they hatch about a week later.\n\nFor centuries, people living along the Karva caught the sturgeon, but it was never mainly for its meat. What they valued most were the eggs of the females, which were salted and sold as caviar, one of the most expensive foods in the world. The meat was eaten locally or simply thrown away. Because caviar can only be taken from mature females, every fish caught for the trade was one that would never breed again.\n\nThe second blow came in the 1960s, when a large hydroelectric dam was built across the middle of the river. It was designed to produce electricity and to supply water for farming, and no one considered the fish. The dam cut the sturgeon off from around 80 per cent of their breeding grounds. Within twenty years, the number of adults returning to the river each spring had fallen by more than nine-tenths.\n\nSerious efforts to protect the species began only in the 1990s. Commercial fishing for sturgeon was banned completely in 2005, and the sale of wild caviar became illegal. The ban has helped, but it has not ended the problem: illegal fishing continues, especially at night, because a single female can still be worth more than a fisherman earns in a year.\n\nEngineers have also tried to give the fish a way past the dam. Building a traditional fish ladder was impossible, as the sturgeon is far too large to jump. Instead, a fish lift was installed in 2016. It works rather like a lock on a canal: fish swim into a chamber at the bottom of the dam, the chamber fills with water, and they are released into the river above. In its first year it carried only a few dozen fish, but numbers have risen steadily since then.\n\nThe third part of the programme is a hatchery, where eggs and sperm taken from adult fish are used to raise young sturgeon. The first young fish were released when they were only a few weeks old, and very few survived. Since then the hatchery has kept them for a full year before releasing them, and their survival rate is many times higher. Some of the people who work at the hatchery and patrol the river at night are former fishermen, who know the river better than anyone.\n\nThere are encouraging signs. More adults are returning to the river each spring, and young sturgeon have been found in places where none had been seen for decades. But biologists warn that the real test is still to come. It will be at least twenty years before the first females raised in the hatchery are old enough to breed, and only then will it be clear whether the Karva sturgeon can survive without human help.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-6. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-6 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"The Karva sturgeon","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Body · covered in rows of bony plates called ___","accept":["scutes"],"limit":1,"evidence":"bony plates known as scutes","why":{"en":"\"Five rows of hard, bony plates known as scutes\": called = known as.","tr":"\"Scute olarak bilinen beş sıra sert, kemiksi plaka\": called = known as.","fa":"«پنج ردیف صفحه‌ی سخت و استخوانی که به آن‌ها scute می‌گویند»: called یعنی known as."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Feeding · sucks up food from the river ___","accept":["bed"],"limit":1,"evidence":"swimming slowly along the river bed","why":{"en":"\"Swimming slowly along the river bed and sucking up whatever it finds there.\"","tr":"\"Nehir tabanı boyunca yavaşça yüzüp orada bulduğu her şeyi emerek.\"","fa":"«آرام در کف رودخانه شنا می‌کند و هر چیزی را که آن‌جا پیدا کند می‌مکد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Feeding · main diet: insect larvae, ___ and shellfish","accept":["worms"],"limit":1,"evidence":"insect larvae, worms and shellfish","why":{"en":"\"Its diet consists mainly of insect larvae, worms and shellfish.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Beslenmesi çoğunlukla böcek larvaları, solucanlar ve kabuklulardan oluşur.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«غذایش بیشتر لارو حشره، کرم و صدف است». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":4,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Breeding · females first breed at about ___ years old","accept":["20"],"limit":1,"evidence":"when they are about 20 years old","why":{"en":"\"About 20 years old\": \"about\" and \"years old\" are printed, so write the number only.","tr":"\"Yaklaşık 20 yaşında\": \"about\" ve \"years old\" yazılı, yalnızca sayıyı yaz.","fa":"«حدود ۲۰ سالگی»: «about» و «years old» چاپ شده‌اند، فقط عدد را بنویس."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":5,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Breeding · travel up to ___ km upstream","accept":["900"],"limit":1,"evidence":"swim up to 900 kilometres upstream","why":{"en":"\"Up to 900 kilometres upstream\". \"km\" is printed.","tr":"\"Akıntıya karşı 900 kilometreye kadar\". \"km\" yazılı.","fa":"«تا ۹۰۰ کیلومتر خلاف جریان». «km» چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":6,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Breeding · eggs are laid on beds of ___","accept":["pebbles"],"limit":1,"evidence":"lay their eggs on beds of pebbles","why":{"en":"\"They lay their eggs on beds of pebbles.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Yumurtalarını çakıl taşı yataklarına bırakırlar.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«تخم‌هایشان را روی بستری از سنگریزه می‌گذارند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 7-13. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 7-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"People caught the Karva sturgeon mainly for its meat.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"it was never mainly for its meat","why":{"en":"\"It was never mainly for its meat\": the eggs were what people valued.","tr":"\"Hiçbir zaman esas olarak eti için değildi\": insanların değer verdiği yumurtalardı.","fa":"«هیچ‌وقت عمدتاً به‌خاطر گوشتش نبود»: چیزی که مردم ارزشش را می‌دانستند تخم‌ها بود."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The dam stopped the fish from reaching most of their breeding grounds.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"around 80 per cent of their breeding grounds","why":{"en":"\"Cut the sturgeon off from around 80 per cent of their breeding grounds\" = most of them.","tr":"\"Mersin balığının üreme alanlarının yaklaşık yüzde 80’iyle bağlantısını kesti\" = çoğu.","fa":"«دسترسی ماهی‌ها را به حدود ۸۰ درصد محل‌های تخم‌ریزی قطع کرد» یعنی بیشترشان."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Since 2005, no sturgeon have been caught illegally.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"illegal fishing continues, especially at night","why":{"en":"The ban \"has not ended the problem: illegal fishing continues\".","tr":"Yasak \"sorunu bitirmedi: yasa dışı avlanma sürüyor\".","fa":"ممنوعیت «مشکل را تمام نکرده: صید غیرقانونی ادامه دارد»."},"trap":["TR-hedge"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The fish lift was paid for by an international organisation.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"a fish lift was installed in 2016","why":{"en":"The text gives the year and how the lift works, but not who paid for it.","tr":"Metin yılı ve asansörün nasıl çalıştığını veriyor ama parasını kimin ödediğini vermiyor.","fa":"متن سال و طرز کار بالابر را می‌گوید، اما نمی‌گوید پولش را چه کسی داد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Young sturgeon survive better if they are kept longer in the hatchery.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"their survival rate is many times higher","why":{"en":"Released at a few weeks, \"very few survived\"; kept for a year, \"their survival rate is many times higher\".","tr":"Birkaç haftalıkken bırakılınca \"çok azı hayatta kaldı\"; bir yıl tutulunca \"hayatta kalma oranları kat kat yüksek\".","fa":"وقتی چندهفته‌ای رها می‌شدند «خیلی کم زنده ماندند»؛ وقتی یک سال نگه داشته شدند «نرخ زنده ماندنشان چندین برابر است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Some former fishermen now help to protect the sturgeon.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"are former fishermen, who know the river better than anyone","why":{"en":"Some of the people who work at the hatchery and patrol the river \"are former fishermen\".","tr":"Kuluçkahanede çalışan ve nehirde devriye gezenlerin bazıları \"eski balıkçılar\".","fa":"بعضی از کسانی که در تکثیرگاه کار می‌کنند و در رودخانه گشت می‌زنند «ماهیگیرهای سابق‌اند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most people living near the Karva support the protection programme.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"There are encouraging signs","why":{"en":"The text reports more fish and a warning from biologists; it says nothing about what local people think.","tr":"Metin daha fazla balıktan ve biyologların uyarısından söz ediyor; yerel halkın ne düşündüğü hakkında bir şey söylemiyor.","fa":"متن از ماهی‌های بیشتر و هشدار زیست‌شناس‌ها می‌گوید؛ درباره‌ی نظر مردم محلی چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]}]}],"id":"c-x06-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The fish feeds along the river bed.\" The river bed is...","options":["the bank of the river","the bottom of the river","the place where the river starts"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The bed of a river is the ground at the bottom of it.","tr":"Nehir yatağı, nehrin dibindeki zemindir.","fa":"بستر رود یعنی زمینِ کف آن."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"A statement says \"The ban has completely solved the problem.\" Which words in a passage would make it FALSE?","options":["the ban has reduced the problem, but it still exists","the ban was introduced ten years ago","the ban is popular"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"It still exists\" contradicts \"completely solved\".","tr":"\"Hâlâ var\", \"tamamen çözdü\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«هنوز وجود دارد» با «کاملاً حل کرده» تناقض دارد."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Note: \"lives for more than ___ years\" (ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER). The passage says \"more than eighty years\". You write...","options":["more than 80","eighty years","80"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"more than\" and \"years\" are printed. Write the number only; 80 or eighty are both one word or number.","tr":"\"more than\" ve \"years\" yazılı. Yalnızca sayıyı yaz.","fa":"«more than» و «years» چاپ شده‌اند. فقط عدد را بنویس."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"A new visitor centre opened in 2019.\" Statement: \"The visitor centre was built with money from local businesses.\"","options":["FALSE","NOT GIVEN","TRUE"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The opening year is given; the source of the money is not.","tr":"Açılış yılı veriliyor; paranın nereden geldiği verilmiyor.","fa":"سال افتتاح آمده؛ منبع پول نیامده."}}],"id":"c-x06-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: listings and a guide","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: ilanlar ve bir rehber","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: فهرست‌ها و یک راهنما"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to match statements to five short listings, using some letters more than once, and to complete a flow-chart with one word from a step-by-step guide.","tr":"Bu derste bazı harfleri birden fazla kullanarak ifadeleri beş kısa ilanla eşleştirmeyi ve adım adım bir rehberden tek kelimeyle bir akış şemasını tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را با پنج آگهیِ کوتاه جور کنی، طوری که بعضی حرف‌ها بیش از یک بار بیایند، و یک نمودار مراحل را با یک کلمه از یک راهنمای قدم‌به‌قدم کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"about 15 min","tr":"yaklaşık 15 dk","fa":"حدود ۱۵ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: family walks and becoming a florist","tr":"Bu sınav: aile yürüyüşleri ve çiçekçi olmak","fa":"این آزمون: پیاده‌روی خانوادگی و گل‌فروش شدن"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 1 uses everyday texts. Adverts and listings for places, events and courses are the most common. A step-by-step guide often comes with a flow-chart: the boxes follow the steps in the text.","tr":"GT Section 1 günlük metinler kullanır. Yerler, etkinlikler ve kurslar için ilanlar en sık çıkanlardır. Adım adım bir rehber çoğu zaman bir akış şemasıyla gelir: kutular metindeki adımları izler.","fa":"GT Section 1 از متن‌های روزمره استفاده می‌کند. آگهی و فهرست برای جاها، رویدادها و دوره‌ها رایج‌ترین‌اند. راهنمای قدم‌به‌قدم اغلب با نمودار مراحل می‌آید: خانه‌ها قدم‌های متن را دنبال می‌کنند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-ads"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-ads","n":24,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 24 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 24’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۴ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Walk listings and a career guide","tr":"Yürüyüş ilanları ve bir kariyer rehberi","fa":"فهرست مسیرهای پیاده‌روی و یک راهنمای شغلی"},"asks":{"en":"Text 1 describes five walks, A-E: you decide which walk matches each statement. Text 2 explains the steps to a job: you complete a flow-chart with one word from the text.","tr":"Metin 1 beş yürüyüşü anlatıyor, A-E: her ifadeye hangi yürüyüşün uyduğuna karar verirsin. Metin 2 bir mesleğe giden adımları açıklıyor: metinden tek bir kelimeyle bir akış şemasını tamamlarsın.","fa":"متن ۱ پنج مسیر پیاده‌روی را توصیف می‌کند، A تا E: تصمیم می‌گیری کدام مسیر با هر جمله جور است. متن ۲ قدم‌های رسیدن به یک شغل را توضیح می‌دهد: یک نمودار مراحل را با یک کلمه از متن کامل می‌کنی."},"fields":["Who the walk suits","Facilities","Rules","Transport","Steps to the job"],"words":[{"a":"suitable for pushchairs","b":"flat and surfaced / good for buggies","tr":"bebek arabasına uygun","fa":"مناسب کالسکه"},{"a":"activity for children","b":"a trail / something to tick off","tr":"çocuklar için etkinlik","fa":"فعالیت برای بچه‌ها"},{"a":"public transport","b":"catch the bus back","tr":"toplu taşıma","fa":"حمل‌ونقل عمومی"},{"a":"on a lead","b":"kept under control","tr":"tasmalı","fa":"با قلاده"},{"a":"free of charge","b":"no entry fee / thanks to a trust","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"local produce","b":"food made or grown nearby","tr":"yerel ürünler","fa":"محصولات محلی"},{"a":"muddy","b":"wet and soft after rain","tr":"çamurlu","fa":"گل‌آلود"},{"a":"way in","b":"a first step into a job","tr":"giriş yolu","fa":"راه ورود"},{"a":"placement","b":"time working in a real workplace during a course","tr":"staj","fa":"دوره‌ی کار عملی"},{"a":"apprenticeship","b":"earn a wage while you train","tr":"çıraklık","fa":"کارآموزی"},{"a":"portfolio","b":"a collection of your best work","tr":"portfolyo","fa":"نمونه‌کار"}],"traps":[{"en":"One walk can match two statements, and one may match none: here five walks share seven statements.","tr":"Bir yürüyüş iki ifadeye uyabilir, biri hiçbirine uymayabilir: burada beş yürüyüş yedi ifadeyi paylaşıyor.","fa":"یک مسیر ممکن است با دو جمله جور باشد و یکی با هیچ‌کدام: این‌جا پنج مسیر هفت جمله را بین خودشان تقسیم می‌کنند."},{"en":"Same word, different meaning: \"a large car park\" and \"a bus stop at the gate\" both describe getting there, but only one is public transport.","tr":"Aynı kelime, farklı anlam: \"büyük bir otopark\" ve \"kapıda bir otobüs durağı\" ikisi de oraya ulaşmayı anlatır ama yalnızca biri toplu taşımadır.","fa":"کلمه‌ی یکسان، معنای متفاوت: «یک پارکینگ بزرگ» و «ایستگاه اتوبوس جلوی در» هر دو درباره‌ی رسیدن به آن‌جا هستند، اما فقط یکی حمل‌ونقل عمومی است."}],"example":{"text":"\"B  Riverside Path: the riverside café is closed in winter, but the toilets at the start are open all year.\"","item":"Which walk has toilets you can use in January?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"The café is closed in winter, but \"the toilets... are open all year\".","tr":"Kafe kışın kapalı ama \"tuvaletler bütün yıl açık\".","fa":"کافه زمستان بسته است، اما «توالت‌ها تمام سال باز است»."}}},{"id":"GT1-ads","ctx":["GT1-ads"],"title":{"en":"Adverts and listings","tr":"İlanlar ve listeler","fa":"آگهی‌ها و فهرست‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"Short adverts or listings A-F for courses, events, campsites, tours or clubs. Questions ask which advert mentions a fact, or whether a statement is TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Kurslar, etkinlikler, kamp alanları, turlar ya da kulüpler için A-F harfli kısa ilanlar veya listeler. Sorular hangi ilanın bir bilgiden söz ettiğini ya da bir ifadenin TRUE, FALSE veya NOT GIVEN olduğunu sorar.","fa":"آگهی‌ها یا فهرست‌های کوتاه A تا F برای کلاس‌ها، رویدادها، کمپ‌ها، تورها یا باشگاه‌ها. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام آگهی به یک نکته اشاره می‌کند، یا یک جمله TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است."},"fields":["Which course is suitable for complete beginners?","Which event takes place outdoors?","Which campsite allows dogs?","Booking is required for all tours."],"words":[{"a":"suitable for beginners","b":"no experience needed","tr":"yeni başlayanlara uygun","fa":"مناسب مبتدی‌ها"},{"a":"free of charge","b":"at no cost / complimentary","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"booking essential","b":"places must be reserved","tr":"rezervasyon şart","fa":"رزرو الزامی"},{"a":"reduced price","b":"discount / 20% off","tr":"indirimli fiyat","fa":"قیمت با تخفیف"},{"a":"family-friendly","b":"children welcome","tr":"aileye uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"},{"a":"outdoors","b":"in the open air","tr":"açık havada","fa":"در فضای باز"},{"a":"pets allowed","b":"dogs welcome","tr":"evcil hayvan kabul edilir","fa":"ورود حیوان خانگی آزاد"},{"a":"on site","b":"at the campsite itself","tr":"tesis içinde","fa":"در خود محل"},{"a":"equipment provided","b":"everything supplied","tr":"ekipman sağlanır","fa":"تجهیزات داده می‌شود"},{"a":"refundable","b":"money back if you cancel","tr":"iade edilebilir","fa":"قابل استرداد"},{"a":"weekly","b":"once a week","tr":"haftalık","fa":"هفتگی"},{"a":"within walking distance","b":"nearby / a short walk away","tr":"yürüme mesafesinde","fa":"با پای پیاده نزدیک"}],"traps":[{"en":"Matching: two adverts mention dogs, but only one allows them. Read the whole line.","tr":"Eşleştirme: iki ilan köpeklerden söz eder ama yalnızca biri izin verir. Satırın tamamını oku.","fa":"جورکردن: دو آگهی از سگ حرف می‌زنند، ولی فقط یکی اجازه می‌دهد. کل خط را بخوان."},{"en":"\"Free\" in one advert may mean free parking, not free entry.","tr":"Bir ilandaki \"free\" giriş değil, ücretsiz otopark anlamına gelebilir.","fa":"«free» در یک آگهی شاید یعنی پارکینگ رایگان، نه ورود رایگان."}],"example":{"text":"C  Lakeside Campsite. Quiet site by the water. Sorry, no dogs. Shop on site.\nD  Hilltop Farm Camping. Families and well-behaved pets welcome. Nearest shop 2 km.","item":"Which campsite allows dogs?","answer":"D","why":{"en":"Both mention dogs or pets. C says \"no dogs\"; D says \"pets welcome\".","tr":"İkisi de köpek ya da evcil hayvandan söz ediyor. C \"köpek yok\", D \"evcil hayvanlar kabul\" diyor.","fa":"هر دو از سگ یا حیوان خانگی حرف می‌زنند. C می‌گوید «سگ ممنوع»؛ D می‌گوید «حیوان خانگی پذیرفته می‌شود»."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-ads"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-ads","n":24,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 24 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 24’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۴ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Seven statements, then a flow-chart","tr":"Yedi ifade, sonra bir akış şeması","fa":"هفت جمله، بعد یک نمودار مراحل"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: which walk, A-E, matches each statement? Some letters are used more than once. Questions 8-14: complete a flow-chart with ONE WORD ONLY from the second text. Aim to finish in about 15 minutes.","tr":"Soru 1-7: her ifadeye A-E’den hangi yürüyüş uyuyor? Bazı harfler birden fazla kullanılır. Soru 8-14: ikinci metinden ONE WORD ONLY ile bir akış şemasını tamamla. Yaklaşık 15 dakikada bitirmeye çalış.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: کدام مسیر، A تا E، با هر جمله جور است؟ بعضی حرف‌ها بیش از یک بار می‌آیند. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۴: یک نمودار مراحل را با ONE WORD ONLY از متن دوم کامل کن. سعی کن در حدود ۱۵ دقیقه تمام کنی."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Scan for meaning, then follow the steps","tr":"Anlam için tara, sonra adımları izle","fa":"دنبال معنی بگرد، بعد قدم‌ها را دنبال کن"},"steps":[{"en":"Turn each statement into one idea (children, bus, dogs, buggy) and scan all five listings for it.","tr":"Her ifadeyi tek bir fikre çevir (çocuklar, otobüs, köpekler, bebek arabası) ve beş ilanın hepsinde onu tara.","fa":"هر جمله را به یک ایده تبدیل کن (بچه‌ها، اتوبوس، سگ، کالسکه) و هر پنج آگهی را برایش مرور کن."},{"en":"For the flow-chart, use the numbered steps in the text to find the right box.","tr":"Akış şeması için doğru kutuyu bulmak üzere metindeki numaralı adımları kullan.","fa":"برای نمودار مراحل، از قدم‌های شماره‌دار متن استفاده کن تا خانه‌ی درست را پیدا کنی."},{"en":"Copy one word exactly; the words around the gap tell you if it is a noun, an adjective or a verb.","tr":"Tek kelimeyi aynen kopyala; boşluğun etrafındaki kelimeler isim mi, sıfat mı, fiil mi olduğunu söyler.","fa":"یک کلمه را دقیقاً کپی کن؛ کلمه‌های دور جای خالی می‌گویند اسم است، صفت یا فعل."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"A letter can be used twice","tr":"Bir harf iki kez kullanılabilir","fa":"یک حرف می‌تواند دو بار بیاید"},"body":{"en":"With five listings and seven statements, at least two letters are used twice. Do not rule out a listing because you have already used it, and read the whole listing: an important detail is often in the last sentence.","tr":"Beş ilan ve yedi ifade olunca en az iki harf iki kez kullanılır. Bir ilanı zaten kullandın diye eleme ve ilanın tamamını oku: önemli bir ayrıntı çoğu zaman son cümlededir.","fa":"با پنج آگهی و هفت جمله، دست‌کم دو حرف دو بار می‌آیند. یک آگهی را فقط چون قبلاً استفاده‌اش کرده‌ای کنار نگذار و کل آگهی را بخوان: جزئیات مهم اغلب در جمله‌ی آخر است."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One flow-chart box, step by step","tr":"Bir akış şeması kutusu, adım adım","fa":"یک خانه‌ی نمودار، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the flow-chart. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer.","text":"\"Step 2: Most bakeries want staff with a basic food hygiene certificate, which you can get online in a day.\"","item":"Step 2: Get a food hygiene ___","answer":"certificate","walk":[{"en":"Use the step number to find the place in the text.","tr":"Metindeki yeri bulmak için adım numarasını kullan.","fa":"با شماره‌ی قدم جایش را در متن پیدا کن."},{"en":"\"food hygiene\" is printed, so the gap needs the noun that follows it.","tr":"\"food hygiene\" yazılı, yani boşluk ondan sonra gelen ismi istiyor.","fa":"«food hygiene» چاپ شده، پس جای خالی اسمی را می‌خواهد که بعدش می‌آید."},{"en":"Write certificate: one word, singular, as in the text.","tr":"certificate yaz: tek kelime, metindeki gibi tekil.","fa":"certificate را بنویس: یک کلمه، مفرد، مثل متن."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Five listings, A-E, and seven statements. You have already used B once. The next statement matches B as well. What do you do?","options":["Use B again","Choose a different letter","Leave it blank"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Letters can be used more than once when there are more statements than listings.","tr":"İfade sayısı ilan sayısından fazlaysa harfler birden fazla kullanılabilir.","fa":"وقتی تعداد جمله‌ها از آگهی‌ها بیشتر است، حرف‌ها می‌توانند بیش از یک بار بیایند."}},"remember":{"en":"Match meanings across all the listings, use letters again when they fit, and follow the numbered steps for the flow-chart.","tr":"Anlamları tüm ilanlarda eşleştir, uyduğunda harfleri yeniden kullan ve akış şeması için numaralı adımları izle.","fa":"معنی‌ها را در همه‌ی آگهی‌ها جور کن، اگر حرفی جور بود دوباره به کارش ببر و برای نمودار مراحل قدم‌های شماره‌دار را دنبال کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"Family walks and a florist’s career","tr":"Aile yürüyüşleri ve çiçekçilik kariyeri","fa":"پیاده‌روی خانوادگی و شغل گل‌فروشی"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-ads"],"texts":[{"title":"Family walks around Ashwell Vale","kind":"listings","body":"A  Millpond Loop (3 km)\nA gentle circuit around the old mill pond, which takes about an hour at a child's pace. The path is completely flat and surfaced all the way round, so it is ideal if you have a pushchair or a buggy. Children love feeding the ducks, and there is a café at the car park where the walk begins and ends.\n\nB  Hazel Wood Trail (5 km)\nThis woodland walk is especially popular with families because of its nature trail: pick up an activity sheet from the box at the gate, and children can tick off the carved animals hidden along the way. The paths can become very muddy after rain, so boots are essential from October to April.\n\nC  Coastguard Path (7 km)\nA dramatic walk along the cliffs, with views of the lighthouse and, on a good day, seals on the rocks below. It is not suitable for children under eight, as some sections are close to the edge. The path ends in Saltby village, where you can catch the number 12 bus back to the start.\n\nD  Orchard Way (4 km)\nThis easy route passes through apple orchards and fields of sheep, so dogs must be kept on a lead at all times. Halfway round there is a picnic area with toilets, and at the end you will find a farm shop selling apple juice, cheese and other local produce.\n\nE  Castle Ridge (6 km)\nThe climb to the ridge is steep, but the reward is worth it: the ruins of Ashwell Castle, which visitors can explore free of charge thanks to a local trust. In summer an ice-cream van parks at the top. Allow at least three hours with young children, and take plenty of water, as there is no shade on the ridge and nowhere to buy drinks outside the summer months."},{"title":"Becoming a florist: a step-by-step guide","kind":"career guide","body":"Working with flowers can be creative and satisfying, but it is also physically demanding. Here is how most people get started.\n\n1 Get some practical experience\nMany flower shops take on extra help at their busiest times, particularly in the weeks before major festivals, and this is often the easiest way in. Shops are often so busy at these times that they are happy to train people with no experience at all. At first you will mainly be preparing flowers: removing leaves, cutting stems and cleaning buckets. It is not glamorous, but it shows you how a shop really works.\n\n2 Consider a qualification\nYou do not need a qualification to work in a shop, but it helps. A one-year college course covers plant care, design and the basics of running a business, and includes a work placement in a local shop. Alternatively, you could look for an apprenticeship, which allows you to earn a wage while you train.\n\n3 Build a portfolio\nEmployers want to see what you can do. Take good photographs of every arrangement you make, whether at college, at work or for friends, and keep them in a portfolio that you can show at interviews.\n\n4 Find your first job\nMost florists work in shops, but there are also jobs in large hotels, which have flowers delivered every day, and in events companies that decorate venues for conferences and parties.\n\n5 Think about the future\nAfter a few years, many florists decide to go freelance, often specialising in weddings, which can be very well paid. You will need a van and a reliable way of finding customers, but you will have far more control over your working life.\n\nBe prepared for early starts: florists usually buy their flowers at a wholesale market that opens at four in the morning, and the workrooms are kept cold to keep the flowers fresh. Make sure you are comfortable with this before you commit to the career."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Look at the five walks, A-E. For which walk are the following statements true? Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E"],"questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"match","prompt":"There is an activity specially for children.","correct":1,"evidence":"pick up an activity sheet from the box at the gate","why":{"en":"B: children tick off carved animals on an activity sheet.","tr":"B: çocuklar bir etkinlik kâğıdında oyma hayvanları işaretliyor.","fa":"B: بچه‌ها روی برگه‌ی فعالیت، حیوان‌های کنده‌کاری‌شده را تیک می‌زنند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"match","prompt":"You can return to the start by public transport.","correct":2,"evidence":"where you can catch the number 12 bus back to the start","why":{"en":"C: \"catch the number 12 bus back to the start\". A has a car park, not public transport.","tr":"C: \"başlangıca dönmek için 12 numaralı otobüse binebilirsin\". A’da otopark var, toplu taşıma değil.","fa":"C: «می‌توانی اتوبوس شماره‌ی ۱۲ را بگیری و به نقطه‌ی شروع برگردی». A پارکینگ دارد، نه حمل‌ونقل عمومی."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":3,"kind":"match","prompt":"Dogs must be kept under control.","correct":3,"evidence":"dogs must be kept on a lead at all times","why":{"en":"D: there are sheep, so \"dogs must be kept on a lead at all times\".","tr":"D: koyunlar var, bu yüzden \"köpekler her zaman tasmalı tutulmalı\".","fa":"D: گوسفند هست، پس «سگ‌ها باید همیشه قلاده داشته باشند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"match","prompt":"This walk is suitable for people with a pushchair.","correct":0,"evidence":"it is ideal if you have a pushchair or a buggy","why":{"en":"A: \"completely flat and surfaced... ideal if you have a pushchair\".","tr":"A: \"tamamen düz ve kaplı... bebek araban varsa ideal\".","fa":"A: «کاملاً هموار و آسفالت... اگر کالسکه داری ایده‌آل است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"match","prompt":"You can visit a historic site without paying.","correct":4,"evidence":"which visitors can explore free of charge","why":{"en":"E: the castle ruins can be explored \"free of charge\".","tr":"E: kale kalıntıları \"ücretsiz\" gezilebiliyor.","fa":"E: از ویرانه‌های قلعه می‌شود «رایگان» بازدید کرد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"match","prompt":"The route can be hard going in wet weather.","correct":1,"evidence":"The paths can become very muddy after rain","why":{"en":"B: \"the paths can become very muddy after rain\". B is used for the second time.","tr":"B: \"yollar yağmurdan sonra çok çamurlu olabiliyor\". B ikinci kez kullanılıyor.","fa":"B: «مسیرها بعد از باران خیلی گل‌آلود می‌شوند». B برای بار دوم استفاده می‌شود."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":7,"kind":"match","prompt":"You can buy food made in the area.","correct":3,"evidence":"a farm shop selling apple juice, cheese and other local produce","why":{"en":"D: \"a farm shop selling... local produce\". The ice-cream van in E is not local produce.","tr":"D: \"yerel ürünler satan bir çiftlik dükkânı\". E’deki dondurma arabası yerel ürün değil.","fa":"D: «یک فروشگاه مزرعه که محصولات محلی می‌فروشد». ون بستنی در E محصول محلی نیست."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 8-14. Complete the flow-chart below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"flow-chart","notesTitle":"Becoming a florist","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Get practical experience: shops need extra help before major ___","accept":["festivals"],"limit":1,"evidence":"particularly in the weeks before major festivals","why":{"en":"\"Particularly in the weeks before major festivals.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Özellikle büyük bayramlardan önceki haftalarda.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«به‌خصوص در هفته‌های قبل از جشن‌های بزرگ». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":9,"kind":"gap","prompt":"First tasks: removing leaves, cutting stems and cleaning ___","accept":["buckets"],"limit":1,"evidence":"cutting stems and cleaning buckets","why":{"en":"\"Removing leaves, cutting stems and cleaning buckets.\"","tr":"\"Yaprakları ayıklamak, sapları kesmek ve kovaları temizlemek.\"","fa":"«کندن برگ‌ها، بریدن ساقه‌ها و تمیز کردن سطل‌ها»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":10,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Take a one-year college course that includes a work ___","accept":["placement"],"limit":1,"evidence":"includes a work placement in a local shop","why":{"en":"\"Includes a work placement in a local shop.\"","tr":"\"Yerel bir dükkânda staj içeriyor.\"","fa":"«شامل یک دوره‌ی کار عملی در یک مغازه‌ی محلی است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"gap","prompt":"OR find an ___ and earn a wage while you train","accept":["apprenticeship"],"limit":1,"evidence":"you could look for an apprenticeship","why":{"en":"\"An apprenticeship, which allows you to earn a wage while you train.\"","tr":"\"Eğitim alırken maaş kazanmanı sağlayan bir çıraklık.\"","fa":"«کارآموزی‌ای که اجازه می‌دهد موقع آموزش دستمزد بگیری»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Keep photographs of your work in a ___","accept":["portfolio"],"limit":1,"evidence":"keep them in a portfolio","why":{"en":"\"Keep them in a portfolio that you can show at interviews.\"","tr":"\"Mülakatlarda gösterebileceğin bir portfolyoda sakla.\"","fa":"«آن‌ها را در یک نمونه‌کار نگه دار که بتوانی در مصاحبه نشان بدهی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"gap","prompt":"First job: in a shop, a large hotel or an ___ company","accept":["events"],"limit":1,"evidence":"in events companies that decorate venues","why":{"en":"\"Events companies that decorate venues for conferences and parties.\" \"company\" is printed.","tr":"\"Konferans ve partiler için mekânları süsleyen etkinlik şirketleri.\" \"company\" yazılı.","fa":"«شرکت‌های برگزاری رویداد که سالن‌ها را برای همایش و مهمانی تزیین می‌کنند». «company» چاپ شده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Later: go ___, often specialising in weddings","accept":["freelance"],"limit":1,"evidence":"many florists decide to go freelance","why":{"en":"\"Many florists decide to go freelance, often specialising in weddings.\"","tr":"\"Birçok çiçekçi serbest çalışmaya karar veriyor, çoğu zaman düğünlerde uzmanlaşarak.\"","fa":"«خیلی از گل‌فروش‌ها تصمیم می‌گیرند آزادکار شوند و اغلب در عروسی‌ها تخصص پیدا می‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x06-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Dogs must be kept on a lead.\" A lead is...","options":["a path for dogs","a dog bowl","a strap or rope attached to a dog"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"A lead keeps a dog close to its owner.","tr":"Tasma köpeği sahibinin yanında tutar.","fa":"قلاده سگ را نزدیک صاحبش نگه می‌دارد."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"You can return by public transport.\" Which words in a listing match?","options":["there is a large car park","catch the bus back to the start","the walk is circular"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A bus is public transport; a car park is not.","tr":"Otobüs toplu taşımadır; otopark değildir.","fa":"اتوبوس حمل‌ونقل عمومی است؛ پارکینگ نیست."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Flow-chart: \"go ___ and work for yourself\" (ONE WORD ONLY). The text says \"decide to go freelance\". You write...","options":["freelance","go freelance","freelancer"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"go\" is printed and the text uses freelance: copy it exactly.","tr":"\"go\" yazılı ve metin freelance kullanıyor: aynen kopyala.","fa":"«go» چاپ شده و متن freelance را آورده: دقیقاً کپی‌اش کن."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Seven statements and five listings, A-E. After six questions you have not used E. What does that tell you?","options":["The last answer must be E","You have made a mistake","Nothing: a letter may not be used at all"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Some letters can be used twice and others not at all; do not force a letter in.","tr":"Bazı harfler iki kez, bazıları hiç kullanılmayabilir; bir harfi zorla yerleştirme.","fa":"بعضی حرف‌ها دو بار و بعضی اصلاً استفاده نمی‌شوند؛ حرفی را به زور جا نده."}}],"id":"c-x06-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
